course: dictionary
lesson: 14031
title: Mandatory: you must do it
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Mandatory is a word for things you have to do. It does not mean "nice to do" or "if you feel like it". When something is mandatory, a rule, a law or a school says you must do it. «Attendance is mandatory on school trips.» Being there is not a choice.
explain: The words around mandatory give you clues. «Fill in every mandatory field on the form.» Forms have boxes you can skip and boxes you cannot. The word mandatory tells you the box must be filled in. Try a test: swap in "you must" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Mandatory often appears in rules and in the law. «Safety goggles are mandatory in the science lab.» The school has made a rule, and everyone in the lab must wear them. In law, a mandatory sentence is a punishment the law says must be given, so the judge has no choice.
fact: Mandatory means required, or something you must do.
fact: Mandatory is a more formal word for compulsory.
fact: «Mandatory» means required by a law or a rule.
fact: Phrases you may see: mandatory for, it is mandatory to, and mandatory field on a form.
fact: In law, a mandatory sentence is a punishment the law says must be given.
exercise: «Wearing a life jacket is mandatory on the boat.» What does mandatory mean? | Only for grown-ups | Optional, you can choose | *Required, you must do it | Very expensive
exercise: «Fill in every mandatory field on the form.» What does this tell you about the boxes? | Pupils can skip them | *You must fill them in | They are decorated | They are only for teachers
exercise: Which word means the same as mandatory? | Forgotten | *Compulsory | Optional | Gentle
test: «Attendance is mandatory on the school trip.» What does mandatory mean here? | Something you may skip | *Something you must do | Something that is free | Something very old
test: What is a mandatory sentence? | *A punishment the law says must be given | A sentence that is optional | A sentence written in capital letters | A short sentence for a test
exam: «Safety goggles are mandatory in the science lab.» Which choice best explains mandatory? | *Something you are required to do by a rule | Something made of glass | Something that is nice to have | Something only the teacher uses
